        "body": "I finished my review and found nothing to comment on. Nice work! :tada:\n\n- Login: the web and device flow now builds its client with `WithoutAuthentication`. The new `--device` test covers a keyring host with no stored token, so my earlier missing-test point is addressed.\n- Docker helper: it builds the default-host client without a token. Each registry lookup reads its own host's credentials, so a registry on another host still works. The new test covers that case, the default host's container registry and its artifact registry.\n- Client: `WithoutAuthentication` skips the token and job-token reads, so a locked keyring cannot fail the build. The new test covers this. Host transport settings (TLS, custom headers) are still applied, and a test checks that.\n- The keyring-missing error only fires in the tokenless default branch, and only when the host's own `use_keyring` is set. The env-token, job-token and `GLAB_USE_KEYRING` cases are covered and I found no regression."
      },
